WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.275
Unit 1 is the guide's Step 5.

2
00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:04.931
Learn's overview, What
is Azure Front Door,

3
00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:10.166
says Front Door is global and sits at the
Microsoft edge with built-in layer three

4
00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:14.384
and four DDoS protection, while
Application Gateway is regional,

5
00:00:14.384 --> 00:00:16.650
in the agency's own virtual network.

6
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.288
Either carries the web application
firewall from Module 2.

7
00:00:20.288 --> 00:00:22.813
The guide's selection is design guidance.

8
00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:27.535
Front Door Premium for internet-facing
applications that need global reach,

9
00:00:27.535 --> 00:00:30.487
Private Link origins or
managed firewall rules.

10
00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:34.914
Application Gateway for regional
applications, for traffic that must enter

11
00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:38.926
through the agency's own network, or
where Front Door isn't in the region.

12
00:00:38.926 --> 00:00:43.284
And both, with Front Door reaching
Application Gateway over Private Link,

13
00:00:43.284 --> 00:00:46.500
where the application needs
regional inspection too.

14
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.874
One date to plan around: Learn's migration
page says classic Front Door retires on

15
00:00:51.874 --> 00:00:54.522
March thirty-first, twenty twenty-seven,

16
00:00:54.522 --> 00:00:57.720
and already accepts no
new profiles or domains.
